statement:
Let $K$ be a field, $V$ a finite-dimensional $K$-vector space [def-weil-finite-dimensional-subspace] of dimension $n=\dim_KV$ [def-weil-vector-space-dimension], $F:V\to V$ a $K$-linear endomorphism, $T$ an indeterminate, and $P(T)=\det(1-TF\mid V)\in K[T]$ [def-weil-polynomial-ring] the reverse characteristic polynomial of $F$ [def-weil-reverse-characteristic-polynomial]. Then:

1. the constant coefficient [def-weil-polynomial-coefficient] of $P$ is $P(0)=1$;

2. $\deg P\leq n$, and the coefficient of $T^n$ in $P$ is $(-1)^n\det(F\mid V)$ [def-weil-endomorphism-determinant];

3. consequently, $\deg P=n$ with leading coefficient $(-1)^n\det(F\mid V)$ if $F$ is invertible, and $\deg P<n$ if $F$ is not invertible.
